{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"3395efaa2dd4790c","name":"card_unit_ki_44_tojo","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/Base/units/card_unit_ki_44_tojo","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"Ki-44 TOJO","text":"Deployment: The enemy discards a random bomber from hand.","flavorText":"The Nakajima Ki-44, code named “Tojo” by the Allies, was a single engine fighter used by the Imperial Japanese Army Air Force during WWII. It first entered service in 1942, and although it was overall a superior combat aircraft compared to its predecessor the Ki-43, it was disliked by pilots due to its poor visibility on the ground, its higher landing speed and restrictions on maneuvering. However, it did have a much better armament than its predecessor, four 12.7mm machine guns or two 12.7mm guns and two 20 mm cannons, instead of only the two 12.7mm machine guns on the Ki-43. Although it was a useful interceptor and could match many Allied fighters capabilities, its performance suffered due the lack of properly trained pilots, which was often the case for the Japanese during the later stages of the war.","faction":"Japan","type":"fighter","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":4,"operationCost":2,"attack":4,"defense":2},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_ki_44_tojo","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_ki_44_tojo_title","SourceString":"Ki-44 TOJO","LocalizedString":"Ki-44 TOJO"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::fighter","attack":4,"defense":2,"range":2,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_ki_44_tojo_text","SourceString":"Deployment: The enemy discards a random bomber from hand.","LocalizedString":"Deployment: The enemy discards a random bomber from hand."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_ki_44_tojo_history","SourceString":"The Nakajima Ki-44, code named “Tojo” by the Allies, was a single engine fighter used by the Imperial Japanese Army Air Force during WWII. It first entered service in 1942, and although it was overall a superior combat aircraft compared to its predecessor the Ki-43, it was disliked by pilots due to its poor visibility on the ground, its higher landing speed and restrictions on maneuvering. However, it did have a much better armament than its predecessor, four 12.7mm machine guns or two 12.7mm guns and two 20 mm cannons, instead of only the two 12.7mm machine guns on the Ki-43. Although it was a useful interceptor and could match many Allied fighters capabilities, its performance suffered due the lack of properly trained pilots, which was often the case for the Japanese during the later stages of the war.","LocalizedString":"The Nakajima Ki-44, code named “Tojo” by the Allies, was a single engine fighter used by the Imperial Japanese Army Air Force during WWII. It first entered service in 1942, and although it was overall a superior combat aircraft compared to its predecessor the Ki-43, it was disliked by pilots due to its poor visibility on the ground, its higher landing speed and restrictions on maneuvering. However, it did have a much better armament than its predecessor, four 12.7mm machine guns or two 12.7mm guns and two 20 mm cannons, instead of only the two 12.7mm machine guns on the Ki-43. Although it was a useful interceptor and could match many Allied fighters capabilities, its performance suffered due the lack of properly trained pilots, which was often the case for the Japanese during the later stages of the war."},"operationCost":2,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Basic","returnSet":"ECardSetEnum::OceaniaStorm","extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Deployment","EHelpBubbleTypes::Ambush"],"hasDeployment":true,"hasAmbush":true,"soundBlowUp":{"ObjectName":"SoundCue'AU_Exp_Aircraft_Medium_Cue'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Card_Blowups/AU_Exp_Aircraft_Medium_Cue.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Japan/t_ki_44_tojo.t_ki_44_tojo","SubPathStri